    "created_at": "2025-09-14T15:10:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-14T15:10:42Z",
    "body": "> When we consider adding new elements, the question of what the AT story is going to be is rather vital and not something we want to skip. Often it goes at the heart of what the actual semantic is. Because if there's no compelling AT story I'd say use the `strong` element, possibly with a `class` attribute.\n\nIt appears that [`<small>` comes with an ARIA role of `generic`](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/#el-small) so I don’t see how `<big>` is different?",
